      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "6639f8669e1b5b3792a8fc06",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Working on content in groups (with multiple contributors), and sharing access to content has always been very complicated in VRChat. There are a lot of situations where some people may want to limit access to worlds or avatars, or distribute the ability to edit them to a very specific number of people. This post is a proposal for features that would allow someone to permit access to upload content to their blueprint ID (and get listed as a contributing author), as well as whitelist access to the content (world or avatar) either within the client, website, or SDK. \n\n**Use Cases:**\n\n• Limiting avatar/world access\n        Making an avatar public allows anyone to wear and use the avatar freely, even those who you would rather not be able to. Simply sharing access to avatars and worlds for your friends, patreon supporters, groups, and server members is complicated and often requires either inviting them to the world yourself, or having them upload the avatar onto their accounts. Having an easy to modify content whitelist would resolve this issue, allowing you to place people you want to have access, and to them, the avatar or world will always be available to them as if it were public, but to others, it will appear as if private.\n• Adding contributors\n        The sharing portion of thise request allows users to be added as contributors rather than only whitelisted. This would grant them a higher level of access to the content, allowing them to update it, modify its information, and be listed as a contributor publicly (or privately if selected) on the asset whether it be a world or an avatar. This helps greatly with crediting users and allows them to all edit the same projects without all needing to log into a shared account.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[Feature Request] Content Sharing & Whitelists",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "63885f34f7308a31d653a04b",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-01T08:00:52.473Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Every world and avatar should automatically get a group to control ownership and leverage permissions.\n\nUse cases:\n\n- Grant admin rights to a commissioned avatar/world while the creator can still edit the project.\n\n- Allow multiple people to upload to the same blueprint ID.\n\n- Allow multiple collaborators to join/edit/upload/publish/unpublish a private avatar/world.\n\n- Control who can do what via permissions.\n\nThere are many possibilities here and I do think groups are perfect for this.\n\nThey may even be a different group type that has no banner or eyecandy features and does not affect the maximum groups created.",
